{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Your brother Israel.</b> What did he see to invoke brotherhood here? Rather, he said to him: We are brothers — sons of Abraham, concerning whom it was said to him: ״כִּי גֵר יִהְיֶה זַרְעֲךָ״ (Genesis 15) — and upon both of us was that debt imposed to pay it (Tanchuma)." "<b>You know all the travail.</b> Therefore your father separated from our father, as it says: ״וַיֵּלֶךְ אֶל אֶרֶץ מִפְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב אָחִיו״ (Genesis 36:6) — because of the tax-collector of the debt imposed upon them; and he cast it upon Jacob."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:44.039815757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}